<article class="env-definition" id="0258">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0258">Definition <span data-tag="0258">41.11.1</span>.</a> Let $A$, $B$ be Noetherian local rings. A local homomorphism $f : A \to B$ is said to be an <em>étale homomorphism of local rings</em> if it is flat and an unramified homomorphism of local rings (please see Definition <a href="/tag/024M" data-tag="024M">41.3.1</a>). </p>
</article>